      "title": "Queues vs Pub/Sub Mental Model",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Queues vs Pub/Sub Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Queue vs Pub/Sub",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Queue",
                "Pub/sub"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Each message goes to",
                  "**one** consumer in a competing group",
                  "**every** subscriber"
                ],
                [
                  "Use for",
                  "work distribution",
                  "fan-out"
                ],
                [
                  "Examples",
                  "SQS, RabbitMQ queue",
                  "SNS, Redis pub/sub, Kafka groups (full copy each)"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Broker and Retention",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Producer",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Broker",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Consumer",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Decoupled in {blue:time}, {green:speed} and {red:failure}",
                "Producer ==does not wait== for the consumer",
                "Queue **deletes** a message after ack",
                "Log (Kafka) **retains** by time/size, so it can be ==replayed=="
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Command vs Event",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Command",
                "Event"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Says",
                  "'do X'",
                  "'X happened'"
                ],
                [
                  "Handled by",
                  "one handler",
                  "any number of listeners"
                ],
                [
                  "Example",
                  "`ChargeCard`",
                  "`OrderPlaced`"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Queue = one consumer per message. Pub/sub = every subscriber. A log keeps messages for ==replay==."
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Interview Point",
              "items": [
                "**Fan-out to many services?** Pub/sub; each subscriber gets a copy.",
                "**Why a broker?** Producer never waits on the consumer.",
                "**Queue vs Kafka log?** Queue deletes after ack; log retains for replay.",
                "**Command vs event?** Command: one handler; event: many listeners."
              ],
              "ink": "orange"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Kafka Basics: Topics, Partitions, Offsets",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Kafka Basics: Topics, Partitions, Offsets",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Topic, partition, offset",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "A **topic** is split into ==partitions==",
                "Each partition is an ==append-only ordered log==",
                "Ordering holds ==only within a partition==, never across",
                "**Offset** = a message's position in its partition",
                "Consumer ==commits offsets== to resume where it left off"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "array",
              "spec": {
                "cells": [
                  "m0",
                  "m1",
                  "m2",
                  "m3",
                  "m4"
                ],
                "indices": true,
                "pointers": [
                  {
                    "index": 3,
                    "label": "committed"
                  }
                ],
                "highlight": [
                  3
                ],
                "caption": "Partition 0: append at the end"
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Keys and consumer groups",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Key is ==hashed== to pick the partition",
                "Same key → same partition → ==order kept==",
                "Each partition is read by ==one consumer== per group",
                "Max parallelism = ==number of partitions=="
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Partitions",
                "Consumers",
                "Result"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "3",
                  "1",
                  "one reads all 3"
                ],
                [
                  "3",
                  "3",
                  "one each"
                ],
                [
                  "3",
                  "4",
                  "{red:1 sits idle}"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Replication",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Each partition has a ==leader== and **followers**",
                "==acks=all== waits for every in-sync replica",
                "With ==min.insync.replicas=2==, losing one broker loses no data"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "properties",
              "lines": [
                "acks=all                # producer",
                "min.insync.replicas=2   # topic/broker"
              ],
              "note": "the durable write setup"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Order needs the **same key**. Parallelism stops at the ==partition count==: extra consumers sit idle."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Delivery Guarantees and Idempotent Consumers",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Delivery Guarantees and Idempotent Consumers",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Commit Order Sets the Guarantee",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Offset commit",
                "Crash means"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "==At-most-once==",
                  "{blue:before} processing",
                  "message {red:lost}, no duplicates"
                ],
                [
                  "==At-least-once==",
                  "{blue:after} processing",
                  "{orange:redelivery}, duplicates possible"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "At-least-once is the ==usual default==",
                "Pair it with an idempotent consumer"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Exactly-Once Is Not Free",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Kafka: ==idempotent producer== (`enable.idempotence=true`) plus **transactions**",
                "Holds only {purple:within Kafka}",
                "External side effects (email, payment API) still need {red:idempotency}"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Idempotent Consumer",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Store the processed **message ID** (unique key or dedupe table)",
                "Skip repeats: the duplicate insert fails",
                "Dedupe check and business write in ==one transaction=="
              ],
              "style": "number"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "sql",
              "lines": [
                "BEGIN;",
                "INSERT INTO processed(msg_id) VALUES ('m42');",
                "UPDATE orders SET status = 'paid' WHERE id = 7;",
                "COMMIT;"
              ],
              "note": "unique key on msg_id"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Operation",
                "Safe to repeat?"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "upsert",
                  "{green:yes}"
                ],
                [
                  "`set status=paid`",
                  "{green:yes}"
                ],
                [
                  "`balance += 10`",
                  "{red:no}"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Default to ==at-least-once + idempotent consumer==. Dedupe outside the write transaction can still double-apply."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Failures: Retries, Dead-Letter Queues and Backpressure",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Failures: Retries, Dead-Letter Queues and Backpressure",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Retry Safely",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Retry only {green:transient} errors: timeouts, 503, throttling",
                "Delay grows ==exponentially==, plus random **jitter**",
                "Set a ==max attempt cap==, then stop retrying",
                "{red:Never} retry in a tight loop"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "delay = min(cap, base * 2 ** attempt)",
                "time.sleep(random.uniform(0, delay))"
              ],
              "note": "full jitter avoids synchronized retry storms"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Dead-Letter Queue",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Receive",
                    "sub": "consumer",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Fails",
                    "sub": "retry again",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "N attempts",
                    "sub": "maxReceiveCount",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "DLQ",
                    "sub": "moved aside",
                    "ink": "red"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "A ==poison message== always fails and blocks the queue",
                "DLQ needs an ==alarm== on its depth",
                "Keep the original payload plus **error metadata**",
                "Have a ==tested redrive== path back to the queue"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Backpressure and Lag",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Lever",
                "Action"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Slow the producer",
                  "throttle, block, return 429"
                ],
                [
                  "Bound the queue",
                  "fixed max size"
                ],
                [
                  "Shed or buffer",
                  "drop low priority, spill to disk"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Consumer lag = ==latest offset - committed offset==",
                "Also watch **queue age**",
                "Scale consumers up to the ==partition count==, no further"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Unbounded queue",
              "text": "A queue that grows without limit only hides overload. ==Bound it== and slow the producer."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Event-Driven Design Pitfalls",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Event-Driven Design Pitfalls",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Event Shape",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Notification",
                "State transfer"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Carries",
                  "`order placed` + ID",
                  "full order data"
                ],
                [
                  "Consumer",
                  "calls back for details",
                  "no callback"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Coordination",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Choreography",
                "Orchestration"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Control",
                  "services react to events",
                  "central coordinator"
                ],
                [
                  "Trade-off",
                  "loose, hard to trace",
                  "explicit flow"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Pitfalls",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "DB + outbox row",
                    "sub": "one transaction",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Relay",
                    "sub": "reads outbox",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Broker",
                    "sub": "publish",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{red:Dual write}: DB and broker written separately, one can be lost",
                "Fix: ==transactional outbox==",
                "Order is ==per key only==, never global",
                "A ==rebalance== mid-processing can reorder handling",
                "Version events: add ==optional fields only==",
                "Old messages stay in the log; consumers upgrade at different times"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Why not write the DB, then publish?** One can fail; use an outbox.",
                "**Is order global?** No, only per key.",
                "**How to evolve schemas?** Add optional fields only."
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Messaging Cheat Sheet",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 5,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Messaging Cheat Sheet",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Pick the Model",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Model",
                "Delivered to",
                "Example"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Queue",
                  "==one== consumer per message",
                  "SQS, RabbitMQ"
                ],
                [
                  "Pub/sub",
                  "==every== subscriber",
                  "SNS, Redis"
                ],
                [
                  "Kafka",
                  "each group gets a full copy; replayable",
                  "partitioned log"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Order holds ==only within a partition== (same key)",
                "Parallelism ≤ ==partition count=="
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Process Safely",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Receive",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Dedupe + write",
                    "sub": "one transaction",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Commit offset",
                    "sub": "after processing",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Default: ==at-least-once== + idempotent consumer",
                "Retry with ==backoff + jitter==, then ==DLQ== with an alarm",
                "Monitor ==consumer lag==: latest minus committed offset"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Design Traps",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "DB write + publish can lose one: use the ==outbox pattern==",
                "==Version== event schemas: add optional fields only"
              ],
              "style": "cross"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Commit the offset **before** processing and a crash loses the message: at-most-once."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Check yourself",
      "role": "quiz",
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Check yourself",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "A consumer charges a card via an API, crashes before committing the offset, then restarts. What happens, and what is the fix?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "Offset uncommitted, so the message is redelivered and the card is charged twice",
                "Pass the message ID as the payment API's idempotency key",
                "Optionally also record the ID in a dedupe table"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "A topic has 4 partitions and the group has 6 consumers. What runs in parallel?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "Only 4 consumers get a partition; 2 sit idle",
                "Max parallelism = partition count"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "Code saves the order to the DB, then publishes an event; it crashes between the two. What breaks?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "Dual write: order saved but event never sent",
                "Fix: write an outbox row in the same transaction; a relay publishes it"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "A poison message fails every time and is retried in a tight loop. What is wrong?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "It blocks the queue and burns CPU",
                "Back off with jitter, cap attempts, then dead-letter it",
                "Alarm on DLQ depth"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
